Product Requirements Document (PRD)
Project: Personal Portfolio Website (Vercel-Hosted Project Showcase)

Owner: Jonathan “Yoni” Schneider
Primary Platform: Next.js (App Router)
Hosting: Vercel
Status: Final Draft v1.1
Goal: High-signal, modern portfolio that showcases real, live products

1. Product Vision

Build a modern, premium portfolio website that showcases multiple production-deployed projects (all hosted on Vercel) in a way that:

Immediately signals technical competence

Feels closer to a product studio / builder portfolio than a resume site

Allows recruiters and mentors to click directly into live, working apps

The site should feel:

intentional

polished

fast

credible

No fluff. No filler.

2. Problem Statement

I have built multiple real applications and analytical projects, each deployed publicly on Vercel:

AI journaling products

A task / productivity app

A fixed income analytics / portfolio site

However:

These projects are scattered across URLs

There is no narrative tying them together

There is no single place that communicates why these projects matter or how I think

This portfolio website solves that by acting as:

A single, curated entry point into my work.

3. Target Users
Primary Users

Recruiters (finance, consulting, analytics, product)

Hiring managers

Partners / senior professionals

Secondary Users

Mentors

Teammates

Other builders / students

4. Core User Journey (Critical)

Desired flow (≤ 30 seconds):

Land on homepage

Immediately see:

who I am

what I build

my best projects

Click a Live Demo (Vercel link)

Understand value + scope in <1 minute

Click resume / LinkedIn

If this works, the product is successful.

5. Scope (MVP)
Pages

Home (primary landing page)

Projects (optional if >5 projects; otherwise sectioned home)

About (short, optional)

No blog, no CMS, no auth.

