7. Project Card Requirements (Key Component)

Each project must have:

Required

Title

One-sentence description (problem → solution)

Tech stack (3–6 tags)

Live Demo link (Vercel)

Visual (screenshot or OG image)

Optional

“Featured” badge

Secondary links (GitHub, PDF, slides)

8. Project Detail View (Modal or Page)

When a project is clicked:

Short overview

What problem it solves

What you built (features)

Tech stack

Outcome / learnings

Links

No long essays. Clear bullets.

9. Design Requirements (Non-Negotiable)
Visual Style

Modern, premium, minimal

Inspired by:

Vercel

Linear

Stripe

Large type

Clean spacing

Strong hierarchy

Motion

Subtle hover states

Soft fade-ins

No gimmicks

Motion should support clarity, not distract

Dark Mode

Strongly preferred

Default or toggle

10. Functional Requirements
FR-1: Project Data Model

Projects stored in a single data file:

title

description

tags

links

featured boolean

image

FR-2: External Links

Live demos open in new tabs

Must support multiple links per project

FR-3: Performance

Static generation

Fast initial load

Lighthouse score target: 90+

11. Non-Functional Requirements

Easy to update (add project in <5 minutes)

No backend

No authentication

Vercel auto-deploy from GitHub

12. Out of Scope (Explicit)

Blog

CMS

Analytics dashboards

Auth

SEO optimization beyond basics

13. Success Criteria

The portfolio is successful if:

A recruiter can open a live app within 20 seconds

The site feels “real” and not academic

Projects feel cohesive, not random

The site elevates your resume rather than repeating it